hnical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI SHIPBUILDING ENG CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI YOSHITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA SHINGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI ZOSEN CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, YOSHITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINGO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI YOSHITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA SHINGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, YOSHITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINGO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of reductively or catalytically decomposing an organochlorine compound such as a dioxin. The method comprises decomposing an organochlorine compound such as a dioxin or o-chloroanisolein an aqueous alkali solution in the presence of a reducing agent or a catalyst. The alkali may be sodium hydroxide, potassium hydroxide, sodium carbonate, potassium carbonate, or ammonia water. The reducing agent may be sodium hydrosulfite, ascorbic acid, hydrazine, hydrazine hydrate, neutral hydrazine sulfate, hydrazine carbonate, sodium thiosulfate, sodium sulfite, potassium sulfite, hydroquinone, the sulfuric acid salt of 4-methylaminophenol, or Rongalit. The catalyst may be activated carbon or titanium oxide.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce procédé de décomposition par réduction ou catalyse d'un composé organochloré tel que la dioxine comprend l'étape consistant à décomposer un composé organochloré, tel que la dioxine ou o-chloroanisole, dans une solution alcaline aqueuse, en présence d'un agent réducteur ou d'un catalyseur. L'alcalin peut être de l'hydroxyde de sodium ou de potassium, du carbonate de sodium ou de potassium, ou de l'ammoniaque. L'agent réducteur peut être un hydrosulfite de sodium, de l'acide ascorbique, de l'hydrazine, un hydrate d'hydrazine, un sulfate d'hydrazine neutre, un carbonate d'hydrazine, du thiosulfate de sodium, du sulfite de sodium ou de potassium, de l'hydroquinone, le sel d'acide sulfurique de 4-méthylaminophénol, ou Rongalit. Le catalyseur peut être du charbon activé ou de l'oxyde de titane.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>